diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 2d935a1..bf5be20 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@ A customizable local social network: profiles you can style (colors, fonts, stic
 - **Release guide:** [docs/RELEASE.md](docs/RELEASE.md) · **Push notifications:** [docs/PUSH_SETUP.md](docs/PUSH_SETUP.md)
 - **Run locally:** `cp .env.example .env`, fill in the Supabase URL and publishable key, `npm i`, `npm run dev`
 - **Local Supabase (Docker, no cloud project needed):** `supabase start` builds the stack and applies every migration plus `seed.sql`; put the printed `API_URL` and `ANON_KEY` into `.env`. Studio: http://127.0.0.1:54323, auth emails (confirm / reset): http://127.0.0.1:54324. `supabase db reset` rebuilds the database from scratch; `supabase stop --no-backup` deletes it. Settings live in `supabase/config.toml`.
-- **Database:** `supabase/migrations/0001…0023` in order, then `supabase/seed.sql`. Each file needs its own numeric prefix — the CLI records one migration version per number. Tests: `npm run test:db` (needs a local Postgres; it uses a mocked Supabase schema and applies every migration in order, so it also catches numbering mistakes). CI runs it on every push.
+- **Database:** `supabase/migrations/0001…0028` in order, then `supabase/seed.sql`. Each file needs its own numeric prefix — the CLI records one migration version per number. Tests: `npm run test:db` (needs a local Postgres; it uses a mocked Supabase schema and applies every migration in order, so it also catches numbering mistakes). CI runs it on every push.
 - **Fonts:** Ubuntu Sans (variable woff2) and its licence are in `public/fonts/`.
 - **Branding:** exact colours and type in [docs/BRANDING.md](docs/BRANDING.md).
 
